      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC, the setup is the following:\n\n```\n * recent 3\n |\n * recent 2\n |\n * recent 1\n |\n | * old 2000\n | |\n | * old 1999\n ...\n | * old 1\n |/\n |\n * target\n```\n\nWhere the commits on the \"recent\" branch have new commit timestamps and low generation numbers and the commits on the \"old\" branch have old commit timestamps and high generation numbers, correct?\n\nThen, due to the ordering in TopoExplorePhase, the \"old\" commits are traversed before the \"recent\" commits due to the higher generation numbers. In the old algorithm (via PendingGenerator), the commits on the \"recent\" branch are popped before the commits on the \"old\" branch due to the more recent commit timestamp. The old algorithm then walks along (and parses) only the \"recent\" branch until it marks \"target\" as uninteresting and exits. TopoSortPendingGenerator also marks \"target\" as uninteresting but only by traversal via the long branch. \n\nI can add a unit test with this scenario, the question is, whether more changes in the topo sorting algorithm are needed and the test should assert no parsing of the commits on the \"old\" branch was done, or if the test should simply measure performance? (and fail above a certain threshold) \n\nTo put it another way: is it acceptable for jgit to parse more commits if a commit graph is active in this case?\n\nI\u0027m asking since command line git also traverses the entire \"old\" branch. For example, in the repository generated by the following (copilot generated) script: https://gist.github.com/flori-schwa/0b42be167887bb61920c4669c9c11c18\n\nRunning `GIT_TRACE2_PERF\u003d1 git -c core.commitGraph\u003dtrue rev-list --topo-order --date-order target ^old ^recent` shows the following topo sorting statistics:\n\n```\nstatistics:{\"count_explore_walked\":2004,\"count_indegree_walked\":2004,\"count_topo_walked\":2}\n```\n\nAlso, I saw that my changes in https://eclipse.gerrithub.io/c/eclipse-jgit/jgit/+/1234062 caused a performance regression which Ivan already addressed in https://eclipse.gerrithub.io/c/eclipse-jgit/jgit/+/1254689. Does the time-out still occur with Ivan\u0027s patch ontop of this change?",
